  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The generated mapping probability surfaces reflect physical building patterns rather than underlying land tenure status, social vulnerability, or household deprivation.",
      "what": "An ensemble of eight city-specific machine learning models trained on open satellite imagery and global building datasets mapped morphological informality across 84 major African cities at 10 m resolution. The framework achieved an independent validation AUC of 0.972, with spatial patterns demonstrating that informal spatial patches under 1 km² comprise up to 72.4% of total detected informal area. A cross-validation against WorldPop 2023 data across 308 community-mapped settlements showed that standard gridded datasets undercounted populations in 89.0% of cases, yielding a median population ratio of just 0.263 relative to ground counts.",
      "why": "Researchers and planners can now detect highly fragmented informal settlements embedded within formal urban fabric across large continental scales, correcting systematic population underestimates in global datasets that miss small-scale informal pockets."
    }
  },
